  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Washington has received $61.6M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The federal government awarded 764 contracts in the state, at an average award size of $80.6K. Obligations fell 99.7% year over year. Fiscal history shows much larger annual totals before FY2027: FY22 reached $12.1B, FY23 reached $13B, FY24 reached $15.4B, FY25 reached $15.8B, and FY26 reached $19.3B. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer so far in FY2027 to date, with $39.2M in obligations, followed by the Department of Health and Human Services with $8.6M and the Department of Energy with $7.5M. T-MOBILE USA, INC. is the largest vendor, with $14.5M in obligations, followed by CAPEX CONSTRUCTION LLC with $11.2M and CAS FSE JV II LLC with $8.9M. Wireless Telecommunications Carriers (except Satellite) is the largest industry by obligations at $14.5M, and Plumbing, Heating, and Air-Conditioning Contractors follows at $11.1M. All figures are contract obligations and FY2027 totals are fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies are buying the most federal contracts in Washington?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $39.2M in FY2027 to date. The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $8.6M, and the Department of Energy obligated $7.5M. The Department of Agriculture obligated $2.5M, and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $1.1M. The Social Security Administration and the Department of Defense each obligated $1M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the largest federal vendors and what industries dominate?",
        "body": "T-MOBILE USA, INC. obligated $14.5M in FY2027 to date, making it the top vendor. CAPEX CONSTRUCTION LLC obligated $11.2M and CAS FSE JV II LLC obligated $8.9M. Wireless Telecommunications Carriers (except Satellite) is the largest industry by obligations at $14.5M, followed by Plumbing, Heating, and Air-Conditioning Contractors at $11.1M and Facilities Support Services at $9M."
      }
    ]
